window.docContents[121].resolve({"/Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels/#Statlib--Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels--Guiding-questions":{"contents":"The roadmap can be organized around the following questions:\n\n* Does there exist a pointwise consistent sequence of decision rules?* Given \\tilde{\\mathcal{P}}_n \\subseteq \\mathcal{P}_n, does there exist a\n  uniformly consistent sequence of decision rules over\n  \\tilde{\\mathcal{P}}_n?* Given \\tilde{\\mathcal{P}}_n \\subseteq \\mathcal{P}_n and a candidate rate\n  r_n(\\tilde{\\mathcal{P}}_n), does there exist a decision rule with that\n  rate of convergence?* If r_n(P_n) is the rate of convergence of T_n at some\n  P_n \\in \\mathcal{P}_n, is there a probability measure \\mathbb{Q} on\n  ([0,\\infty],\\mathcal{B}([0,\\infty])) such that\n\nP_n \\circ\n   \\left(r_n(P_n)\\ell_n(X_n,\\Psi_n(P_n))\\right)\n   \\rightsquigarrow \\mathbb{Q}\n\nas n \\to \\infty?\n\n\n","context":"Statlib\u0009Statistical Risk and Markov Kernels","header":"2.5. Guiding questions","id":"/Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels/#Statlib--Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels--Guiding-questions"}});